WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.136
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to the attic.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.804
Now, as some of you know,
I have been dealing

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.506
with a wasp infestation up here
while I've been taping the show.

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:10.343
There was even a flyby last
week.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.045
It got so bad that I said to
myself,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.812
"If there's a pest worse than
wasps,

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:15.548
I'd love to know what it is.
And lo and behold,

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.083
I opened
<i> The New York Times</i> on Saturday

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.987
to read "'Murder Hornets'
in the U.S."

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.655
Murder. Hornets.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:26.125
Thank you for giving us the
uplifting non-COVID-related news

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.627
we've all been looking for,
<i> New York Times.</i>

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.630
Anyway, story gave me a whole
new appreciation

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.733
for my nonlethal wasps who I'm
almost certain

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.201
aren't murder hornets
in disguise,

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.503
although one of them keeps
telling me I'm pretty

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.071
and bringing me trinkets.
And based on every

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.940
true crime doc I've watched on
Netflix,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.775
that is a red flag.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:45.845
But to thank them for not being
murder hornets,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.981
I have added a few of the wasps
to the writing staff,

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:52.919
which we think will help give
the show some good buzz.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.620
I told you that joke was a dud,
Charlie.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.355
Put your stinger away, Charlie.

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:59.091
Not today. It's Monday.
What?

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:01.827
Oh, Mondays aren't considered
bad by wasps?

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:03.363
Why's that?
Oh, yeah...

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.964
You don't classically have jobs.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.800
Anyway, speaking of duds...
Segue!

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.268
...President Trump gave a town
hall on Fox News last night

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.704
as a damning new report details
how he's wasting time

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.772
he could've been using to
develop a strategy

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:15.374
for safely reopening the
economy.

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:17.544
For more on this, it's time for
A Closer Look.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.016
President Trump beamed into
America's living rooms

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.918
last night during a Fox News
town hall

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:28.654
from the Lincoln Memorial, where
it kind of looked like

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.891
Lincoln had been asked to join
but was keeping his distance.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.993
Now, obviously the interviewers
were practicing

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.829
social distancing there, but
it's more fun if you imagine

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:39.265
they all started out sitting
close together

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.567
and then just scooted their
chairs back a little

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.535
every time Trump said something
insane.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:45.237
"Uh-huh. Oh, interesting.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:48.974
So just...any...household
disinfectant will work.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:51.510
That is... [straining] great
to hear."

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.046
And sure enough, Trump made it
awkward at one point

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:56.649
by pointing to the memorial and
complaining,

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.950
as he has before,

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.887
that he -- he has been treated
worse than Lincoln.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:04.556
-I am greeted with a hostile
press,

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:07.660
the likes of which no president
has ever seen.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.063
The closest would be that
gentleman right up there.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.164
They always said, "Lincoln --
nobody got treated

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:13.866
worse than Lincoln."

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:15.968
I believe I am treated worse.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.505
-You have two unfiltered
hours on national television

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.574
to say whatever you want
to millions of people

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.042
without fact checking or
follow-ups.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.110
Lincoln couldn't even get
through a play

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.213
without being interrupted.

00:02:28.213 --> 00:02:30.917
I'm shocked the memorial didn't
pull a Fauci.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.418
And of course, as is his wont,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.687
Trump rambled incoherently
about God-knows-what

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.188
for basically the entire two
hours

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:38.791
with virtually no attempt
at fact checking

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.059
or rigorous cross-examination
from the moderators.

00:02:41.059 --> 00:02:44.330
I guess Lincoln wasn't the only
statue there last night.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.133
As usual, the Fox moderators let
him lie freely

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.702
about a bunch of verifiably
untrue things

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.370
and in some cases, they didn't
even make him

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.239
answer the question he was
asked.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.142
They were less like reporters
and more like the audience

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.310
in an improv show.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.344
"[ As Trump ] Okay to get
started?

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.613
I just need a one-word
suggestion."

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.982
"Oh, uh, ventilators!"
"That's good.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.418
I think ventilators will be
good."

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.253
Watch him totally lose his train
of thought

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.655
and wander away from a
question that was supposed to be

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.323
about the coronavirus.

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:13.659
-Do you think the election
will come down to a referendum

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:16.362
on how you handled this crisis?
-No, but it's gonna be a factor.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.164
-Do you think it'll be
bigger than that?

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.300
-No. I think the election's
gonna come down to --

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.668
I hope it does because we've
done a great job.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.003
We had no ventilators.
We had no testing.

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:28.307
We had nothing.
I had -- I inherited empty --

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.375
empty -- no ammunition.

00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:31.511
Our military was bad.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.312
We've rebuilt our military.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.981
$1.5 trillion.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.216
We have the best military by far
in the world.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.184
It's rebuilt.
It's either all new

00:03:39.184 --> 00:03:41.720
or the equipment's coming in,
which is great.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.856
-What are you talking about?
Is someone shining

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.625
a laser pointer on the floor
that's distracting you?

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.528
You were asked a question about
the coronavirus,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:51.363
and you said you inherited no
ammunition,

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:54.867
which is both not relevant and
also a ridiculous lie.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.069
You expect everyone to believe
that when you took office,

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.271
soldiers were patrolling war
zones without bullets?

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.439
[ As Trump ] We had no
ammunition.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.107
Whenever a soldier shot a gun,

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:05.278
a little flag popped out that
said, "Thanks, Obama."

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.945
[ Normal voice ] And then,
of course, there were

00:04:06.945 --> 00:04:08.781
the typical nonsensical
Trumpisms

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:12.017
where he tries to make himself
sound like a tactical genius

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:14.520
but reaches for the
dumbest metaphor possible,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.089
like when he was asked if he
would impose new tariffs

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:19.491
on China and said this --

00:04:19.491 --> 00:04:21.460
-We're all playing a very
complicated game

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.829
of chess or poker.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.498
Name whatever you want to name,

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.700
but it's not checkers,
that I can tell you.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.069
-Oh, it's chess<i> or</i> poker?

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.337
You should probably find out
which game it is.

00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:34.206
[ As Trump ] I see you've taken
my rook, but perhaps

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:38.577
these three Jacks will have
something to say about that.

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:41.480
And that something is Uno.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.949
[ Normal voice ] So Trump spent
his Sunday night

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.017
embarrassing the Lincoln
memorial on Fox News,

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:47.587
which makes sense because he's
constantly

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:50.223
in a state of either watching
Fox or appearing on Fox

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.090
or watching himself appearing on
Fox.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:55.061
Eventually, Fox is just gonna
turn into a 24/7 feed

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:58.531
of Trump watching himself on Fox
like an infinity mirror.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.734
Trump also surrounds himself
with people he sees on Fox

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.136
from informal advisers
to White House aides,

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.772
like his newest press secretary
Kayleigh McEnany,

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:08.774
who held her first briefing on
Friday.

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:12.078
and McEnany's hiring very much
illustrates the feedback loop

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:13.845
of disinformation and propaganda

00:05:13.845 --> 00:05:16.749
that exists between the Trump
White House and Fox News.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:19.652
For example, in late February
and early March,

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.422
more than a month after the
first confirmed case

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:23.889
Of coronavirus in the U.S.,

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.692
McEnany went on Fox channels as
a spokesperson

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:29.495
for the Trump campaign and told
outlandish lies

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.930
about Trump's response to
the coronavirus outbreak.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.799
-This president will always
put America first.

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:35.601
He will always protect American
citizens.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.103
We will not see diseases like
the coronavirus come here.

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:41.074
-Let's turn it to your rallies,
the President's rallies.

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.174
Are you a little bit worried

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.710
about holding those kind of
rallies?

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.046
-I'm not, because we have the
added advantage here

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.382
at the Trump campaign that our
candidate happens to be

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.116
the President
of the United States.

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:53.619
-The President goes ahead with
holding his rallies,

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.522
his top doctor --
top medical guy -- says,

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.491
"Don't go with big crowds."

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:02.662
I mean, you're immediately gonna
be hit with this.

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:05.764
-Look, the President is the
best authority on this issue.

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:08.234
-I think what's going on
here is she's playing checkers

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.069
and the interviewer is
playing chess.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.537
Or poker.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.906
Not only is Trump not the best
authority on this,

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.808
whenever he's around actual
authorities,

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.509
they have to keep correcting
him.

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:19.779
My favorite examples of this are
when Trump pitches

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:23.082
insane coronavirus cures, and
the medical experts around him

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:26.018
have to politely tell him, no,
that's not a thing.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:30.556
-Deborah, have you ever heard
of the heat and the light

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:35.127
relative to certain viruses,
yes, but relative to this virus?

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:36.695
-Not as a treatment.

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:38.764
-You take a solid flu vaccine,

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:40.266
you don't think that would have
an impact

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:43.936
or much of an impact on corona?
-No.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:46.572
-Even the real housewives know
there's stuff

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:48.508
you talk about when the
cameras aren't rolling.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:50.443
I mean, they have briefings

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.378
before they have the press
conferences,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:54.080
and I bet they've begged Trump

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.514
to get his dumb
questions out then.

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:57.850
"Hey, before we go out in front
of the American people

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.219
and all those cameras, are there
any, you know, miracle cures

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:01.821
you want to ask us about now?"

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.890
"[ As Trump ] No, no, I had two
out there.

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.291
I got some good ones today."

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:08.827
Here's a hint --
hair spray and Altoids.

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:10.296
Who knows?

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:13.999
Who knows until you say it out
loud in front of the cameras?"

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:15.534
[ Normal voice ] In fact,
Trump's fixation

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.069
on miracle cure-alls and
shortcuts

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.772
is also reflected in a damning
new report

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.774
in<i> The Washington Post</i>
detailing a lost month

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.342
of desperation and dysfunction

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.077
in which he ignored
and then abandoned

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.479
the goal of actually beating
back the virus and instead

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:29.982
focused on prematurely reopening
the economy

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.150
without a plan to do so safely.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:35.688
For example,<i> The Post</i> reports
that Trump was pushed privately

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:38.691
by political allies like
Rudy Giuliani and Fox News hosts

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:41.293
to embrace the drug
hydroxychloroquine

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.862
as a treatment for coronavirus

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:45.497
even though it was unproven and
potentially dangerous.

00:07:45.497 --> 00:07:47.333
That's right,
hydroxychloroquine.

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.268
Remember when everyone cared
about that for a second,

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.737
the Tamagotchi of COVID cures?

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.039
Well, according to<i> The Post,</i>
night after night,

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:55.641
in late March and early April,

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:58.644
he kept hearing about the
controversial antimalarial drug

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.713
on his favorite Fox News channel
programs

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:03.182
where television doctors
and commentators

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.883
touted its efficacy.

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:08.320
Yeah, the TV President who
played a TV businessman

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.458
is listening to TV doctors like
Dr. Oz and Dr. Phil,

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:15.494
seen here getting an X-ray in
real time, I guess.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:16.695
Oof, looks like he took

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.097
the President's advice
on heat and light.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:20.299
Seriously, what's up with the
aggressive blue?

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:23.001
Looks like a spaceship had its
lights on in the parking lot.

00:08:23.001 --> 00:08:25.670
This is what the TSA agent sees
on the monitor

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:26.972
when a normal person goes
through

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:28.908
the airport body scanner.

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:30.977
But there's apparently one
Fox host in particular

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:33.512
that has Trump's ear on
coronavirus issues

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:36.048
and has actually advised him
at the White House.

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:37.984
On April 3rd, Fox host
Laura Ingraham

00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:39.852
paid Trump a visit
in the Oval Office

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.687
to talk up hydroxychloroquine.

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:44.123
She brought with her two regular
on-air guests

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:46.659
and what she dubs
her medicine cabinet.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:49.395
On April 14, Ingraham returned
to the Oval Office

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:50.429
to meet with the President.

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.164
The Fox host reiterated her
belief

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:55.234
that the country needed
to open and argued for limits

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:56.869
on contact tracing.

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:59.071
So a Fox host with no medical
expertise

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:01.941
is directly advising the
President on a deadly pandemic

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:04.844
while that same President hires
pundits he sees on TV

00:09:04.844 --> 00:09:08.213
and fires or punishes actual
experts and inspector generals

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:10.115
who criticize him.
This is what you get

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:11.550
when you make a TV star
President

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:15.020
because when you're on TV, no
one ever tells you you're wrong.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.922
For example, no one ever thought
to tell me

00:09:16.922 --> 00:09:19.525
that I should maybe buy a shirt
in a shade that isn't blue.

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.526
But that's what happens when
you're on TV.

00:09:21.526 --> 00:09:24.397
90% of your agent's job is to
text you after every show

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:25.698
and tell you you're crushing it.

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:27.933
I mean, It's different for me
because, you know,

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:30.369
90% of the time I'm -- you know,
I'm crushing it.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.270
But I meant for other people on
TV, it gives you

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:34.139
a false sense of yourself,
and in Trump's case,

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:36.809
I'm assuming he had an entire
team of producers on-set

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:39.111
to tell him his bronzer
looked realistic

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:41.146
and then air brush whatever
the hell this is

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:43.548
so he doesn't go on TV looking
like he went to the beach

00:09:43.548 --> 00:09:45.751
wearing a football helmet.
And Ingraham's criticism

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.386
of the age-old public health
practice

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:49.855
of contact tracing is especially
worrisome

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:52.457
because it's one of the main
tools experts agree

00:09:52.457 --> 00:09:53.892
we're gonna need to contain
this mess

00:09:53.892 --> 00:09:55.361
and safely reopen things.

00:09:55.361 --> 00:09:57.863
We have to test people
on a massive scale,

00:09:57.863 --> 00:10:00.298
isolate cases, and trace their
contacts

00:10:00.298 --> 00:10:01.634
to see where the outbreaks are.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:03.735
Lots of other major countries
and several states

00:10:03.735 --> 00:10:05.303
like New York are beginning to
do this.

00:10:05.303 --> 00:10:08.240
And contact tracing is a thing
we've already done successfully

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:11.577
for decades for things like
tuberculosis, measles,

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:13.312
and sexually transmitted
infections.

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:14.914
And yet, during a segment that
Trump probably saw,

